    <!--
      Shown ONLY when the tap-and-hold selection breaks the rule (exactly one
      action). Deliberately not a permanent hint: the sheet stays quiet until it has
      something to say.
    -->
    <string name="gesture_hold_rule">Tap and hold cycles, so pick no action or at least two.</string>

    <!--
      The status line, and it must stay TRUE. It used to say the selections were
      stored on the phone only, because the `function` enum was unknown; that is no
      longer the case, so leaving it would be a plain lie on screen. The `function`
      bytes are now measured (see GestureAction) and a change IS written to the buds.
      The second sentence stays because the hold really is a special case: all four
      ANC modes share ONE byte, so the buds decide what the cycle contains.
    -->
    <string name="gesture_write_note">Changes are sent to the earbuds, then read back to confirm. Tap and hold is sent as the earbuds\' own ANC cycle, so which modes it steps through is decided by the earbuds, not here.</string>

